# The backplane computer (hw/design.md), as far as the emulator models it:
# the CPU and north bridge card, 1 MB of RAM on the backplane, and the
# flash. Step 1 of the emulator plan; the cards come later.
#
# The north bridge maps the CPU's 64 KB through four 16 KB windows. At reset
# W0-W2 are RAM blocks 0-2 and W3 is the top 16 KB of ROM A, read-only, so
# the BIOS starts in flash and shadows itself into bank F (hw/design.md,
# "Boot"). Its registers are at $C680. Add `bootsel` to start with W3 on RAM
# block 63 instead, as when the bus spy has loaded RAM.
#
# The flash image is the whole 512 KB ROM A (as a programmer would write
# it), with the BIOS in its top 16 KB: block 31, $7C000-$7FFFF. The CPU
# sees $C800-$FFFF of it; $C000-$C7FF is the I/O hole.
#
# The DMA controller (module 8, $C400) takes the bus from the CPU for its
# transfers; CONTROL starts at $70, so software turns it on. No card that
# requests DMA is modelled yet; memory-to-memory copies work.
#
# The Console card (module E, $C700) is the front panel: switches, lights,
# HALT/CONT and a breakpoint on any bus cycle. Without a panel attached (the
# terminal emulator has none) programs can still use its breakpoint and
# HALT, which stop at the debugger.
#
# The video card (module 9, $C480) draws VGA 640x480 from banks 8-B, which
# it snoops; so far its text and mono layers (video_card.h). It powers up
# with the display off: software sets the palette, a layer and CTRL.
# `emulator --screen FILE` saves its last frame.
#
# The terminal is a STAND-IN: a 6551 in the serial card's I/O block
# ($C300, module 6) until the TL16C552A is modelled.
#
#   emulator --machine machines/backplane.machine --rom bios.rom

cpu          w65c02s
northbridge  backplane

ram   00000-3FFFF  module=0  name=ram_a     # RAM A-D: 256 KB each, A18-A19
ram   40000-7FFFF  module=1  name=ram_b
ram   80000-BFFFF  module=2  name=ram_c
ram   C0000-FFFFF  module=3  name=ram_d
rom   00000-7FFFF  space=flash  module=4  name=rom_a  bios.rom

acia6551  300-37F  space=io  name=terminal  irq     # stand-in serial card
dma       400-47F  space=io  name=dma  irq
video     480-4FF  space=io  name=video  irq
console   700-77F  space=io  name=console  irq     # the front panel
